/-!
# Triangular quasi-quadratic systems

A *triangular quasi-quadratic* (TQ) system over a group `G` is a finite system of equations
`S = S₁ ∪ ⋯ ∪ Sₙ` in disjoint finite tuples of variables `X₁, …, Xₙ`, in which the equations `Sᵢ`
of the `i`-th level involve only the variables `Xᵢ, …, Xₙ`, and, viewing the lower variables
`Xᵢ₊₁, …, Xₙ` as coefficients, each level is of one of four kinds:

1. a standard quadratic equation in `Xᵢ`;
2. the commutation equations `[x, y] = 1` and `[x, c] = 1` for `x, y ∈ Xᵢ` and `c` in a specified
   finite set of words in `G` and the lower variables (the level of an extension of a centralizer);
3. the commutation equations `[x, y] = 1` for `x, y ∈ Xᵢ`;
4. no equations.

The raw lower groups are the coordinate groups `Gᵢ₊₁ = G_{R(Sᵢ₊₁, …, Sₙ)}` of the lower systems,
with radicals taken over `G`, and `Gₙ₊₁ = G`. The system is *nondegenerate* (an NTQ system) when
each level `Sᵢ`, with the lower variables read as the corresponding elements of `Gᵢ₊₁`, has a
solution in `Gᵢ₊₁`. This is a condition level by level, in the raw lower groups; no
discrimination or irreducibility property of the coordinate group of the whole system is part of
it.

Here a system is built from the bottom level up: `System.nil` has no levels and no variables, and
`System.cons S X L` puts a level `L` in new variables `X`, with coefficients in `G[Y]`, on a
system `S` in the variables `Y`; its variables are `X ⊕ Y`. Commutators are Mathlib's
`⁅x, y⁆ = x y x⁻¹ y⁻¹`; only their vanishing matters.

Over a fixed lower group `H`, a centralizer level extends the full centralizer `C_H(u)` of an
element `u` by `ℤⁿ`. `IsAdmissibleCentralizerLevel u U n` records the conditions on such data:
`u` is not a proper power (so `u ≠ 1`), `C_H(u)` is abelian and generated by the finite set `U`,
and the added rank `n` is positive. A raw level of type (2) carries no such conditions.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.LimitGroup.NTQ.Level K X`: the four kinds of level in the variables `X` over
  coefficients `K`, with `Level.equations`.
* `TauCeti.LimitGroup.NTQ.System G Y`: a raw TQ system over `G` in the variables `Y`, with
  `System.equations` and its coordinate group `System.CoordGroup`.
* `TauCeti.LimitGroup.NTQ.System.IsNondegenerate`: every level is solvable in its raw lower group.
* `TauCeti.LimitGroup.NTQ.IsAdmissibleCentralizerLevel u U n`: admissible full-centralizer data.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.LimitGroup.NTQ.System.mem_V_cons`: a solution of `cons S X L` is a solution `w` of `S`
  together with a solution of the top level `L` whose coefficients are evaluated at `w`.
* `TauCeti.LimitGroup.NTQ.System.finite_equations`: a TQ system is a finite system.
* `TauCeti.LimitGroup.NTQ.System.coordGroupNilEquiv`: the raw lower group of the bottom level
  is `G`.
* `TauCeti.LimitGroup.NTQ.System.isNondegenerate_cons_centralizer`,
  `TauCeti.LimitGroup.NTQ.System.isNondegenerate_cons_abelian`,
  `TauCeti.LimitGroup.NTQ.System.isNondegenerate_cons_empty`: levels of types (2)–(4) are solved
  by the trivial point, so only the quadratic levels can make a system degenerate.
* `TauCeti.LimitGroup.NTQ.not_isNondegenerate_commutator_eq_basis`: over `F(a, b)`, the one-level
  system `[x, y] = a` is degenerate, by abelianization.
* `TauCeti.LimitGroup.NTQ.normalClosure_lt_Rad_commute_basis`: over `F(a, b)`, the radical of the
  nondegenerate one-level system `[x, a] = [x, b] = 1` is strictly larger than the normal closure
  of its equations; its centralizer data `u = 1` is not admissible
  (`TauCeti.LimitGroup.NTQ.not_isAdmissibleCentralizerLevel_one`).
* `TauCeti.LimitGroup.NTQ.isNondegenerate_conj_over_commute`: the two-level system with lower
  level `[u, v] = 1` and upper level `x⁻¹ u x u⁻¹ = 1` is nondegenerate.
* `TauCeti.LimitGroup.NTQ.isAdmissibleCentralizerLevel_freeGroup_of`: a basis element of a free
  group, with its own singleton, is admissible centralizer data in every positive rank.

## References

* [IFT] O. Kharlampovich, A. Myasnikov, *Implicit function theorem over free groups*, J. Algebra
  290 (2005), §7.6, Definition 43.
* [VAR-II] O. Kharlampovich, A. Myasnikov, *Irreducible affine varieties over a free group. II:
  Systems in triangular quasi-quadratic form and description of residually free groups*,
  J. Algebra 200 (1998), §0, Definition 8.
* [VAR-I] O. Kharlampovich, A. Myasnikov, *Irreducible affine varieties over a free group. I:
  Irreducibility of quadratic equations and Nullstellensatz*, J. Algebra 200 (1998), §1,
  Definitions 5 and 9.
-/

public section

open Monoid.Coprod Subgroup TauCeti.GroupAlgGeom
open scoped commutatorElement

universe u v

namespace TauCeti.LimitGroup.NTQ

/-! ### Levels -/

/-- A level of a triangular quasi-quadratic system in the variables `X`, with coefficients in a
group `K`; for a system over `G` with lower variables `Y`, the coefficients are the words
`K = G[Y]` in `G` and `Y`. -/
inductive Level (K : Type u) [Group K] (X : Type v) : Type (max u v)
  /-- Type (1): a standard quadratic equation in the variables `X` over `K`. -/
  | quadratic (Q : Quadratic.Standard K X)
  /-- Type (2): `[x, y] = 1` and `[x, c] = 1` for all `x, y ∈ X` and all `c` in a finite set
  `U ⊆ K`, the level of an extension of a centralizer. -/
  | centralizer (U : Set K) (hU : U.Finite)
  /-- Type (3): `[x, y] = 1` for all `x, y ∈ X`. -/
  | abelian
  /-- Type (4): no equations. -/
  | empty

namespace Level

variable {K H X : Type*} [Group K] [Group H]

/-- The equations of a level, as a subset of `K[X]`. -/
def equations : Level K X → Set (GX K X)
  | quadratic Q => {Q.toWord}
  | centralizer U _ =>
    (Set.range fun p : X × X ↦ ⁅(inr (FreeGroup.of p.1) : GX K X), inr (FreeGroup.of p.2)⁆) ∪
      Set.range fun p : X × U ↦ ⁅(inr (FreeGroup.of p.1) : GX K X), inl (p.2 : K)⁆
  | abelian =>
    Set.range fun p : X × X ↦ ⁅(inr (FreeGroup.of p.1) : GX K X), inr (FreeGroup.of p.2)⁆
  | empty => ∅

@[simp]
theorem equations_quadratic (Q : Quadratic.Standard K X) :
    (quadratic Q).equations = {Q.toWord} := (rfl)

theorem equations_abelian :
    (abelian : Level K X).equations =
      Set.range fun p : X × X ↦ ⁅(inr (FreeGroup.of p.1) : GX K X), inr (FreeGroup.of p.2)⁆ :=
  (rfl)

/-- The equations of a level of type (2) are those of type (3) together with the commutators of
the variables with the coefficients in `U`. -/
theorem equations_centralizer (U : Set K) (hU : U.Finite) :
    (centralizer U hU : Level K X).equations = (abelian : Level K X).equations ∪
      Set.range fun p : X × U ↦ ⁅(inr (FreeGroup.of p.1) : GX K X), inl (p.2 : K)⁆ := (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem equations_empty : (empty : Level K X).equations = ∅ := (rfl)

/-- A level in finitely many variables consists of finitely many equations. -/
theorem finite_equations [Finite X] (L : Level K X) : L.equations.Finite := by
  cases L with
  | quadratic Q => exact Set.finite_singleton _
  | centralizer U hU =>
    have := hU.to_subtype
    exact (Set.finite_range _).union (Set.finite_range _)
  | abelian => exact Set.finite_range _
  | empty => exact Set.finite_empty

variable {ι : K →* H} {v : X → H}

/-- The solutions of an abelian level are the tuples of pairwise commuting elements. -/
theorem mem_V_abelian : v ∈ V ι (abelian : Level K X).equations ↔ ∀ x y, Commute (v x) (v y) := by
  simp only [equations_abelian, mem_V, Set.forall_mem_range, Prod.forall, map_commutatorElement,
    eval_inr, FreeGroup.lift_apply_of, commutatorElement_eq_one_iff_commute]

/-- The solutions of the level of an extension of a centralizer are the tuples of pairwise
commuting elements commuting with the coefficients `c ∈ U`. -/
theorem mem_V_centralizer {U : Set K} {hU : U.Finite} : v ∈ V ι (centralizer U hU).equations ↔
    (∀ x y, Commute (v x) (v y)) ∧ ∀ x, ∀ c ∈ U, Commute (v x) (ι c) := by
  rw [equations_centralizer, V_union, Set.mem_inter_iff, mem_V_abelian]
  simp only [mem_V, Set.forall_mem_range, Prod.forall, Subtype.forall, map_commutatorElement,
    eval_inr, eval_inl, FreeGroup.lift_apply_of, commutatorElement_eq_one_iff_commute]

end Level

/-! ### Raw triangular quasi-quadratic systems -/

/-- A raw triangular quasi-quadratic system over `G` in the variables `Y`, built from the bottom
level up. The system `nil` has no levels and no variables; `cons S X L` puts the level `L`, in
finitely many new variables `X` and with coefficients the words `G[Y]` in `G` and the variables
`Y` of the lower system `S`, on top of `S`. -/
inductive System (G : Type u) [Group G] : Type v → Type (max u (v + 1))
  /-- The system with no levels and no variables. -/
  | nil : System G PEmpty
  /-- The system with top level `L` in the variables `X` over the lower system `S`. -/
  | cons {Y : Type v} (S : System G Y) (X : Type v) [Finite X] (L : Level (GX G Y) X) :
      System G (X ⊕ Y)

namespace System

variable {G H : Type*} [Group G] [Group H]

/-- The equations of a raw TQ system, as a subset of `G[Y]`. Those of `cons S X L` are the
equations of `S`, in the lower variables `Sum.inr`, and the equations of the top level `L`, in
the variables `Sum.inl` and with their coefficients `G[Y]` read in `G[X ⊕ Y]`. -/
def equations : {Y : Type v} → System G Y → Set (GX G Y)
  | _, nil => ∅
  | _, cons S _ L =>
    Monoid.Coprod.map (.id G) (FreeGroup.map Sum.inr) '' S.equations ∪
      eval (Monoid.Coprod.map (.id G) (FreeGroup.map Sum.inr))
        (fun x ↦ inr (FreeGroup.of (Sum.inl x))) '' L.equations

@[simp]
theorem equations_nil : (nil : System G PEmpty).equations = ∅ := (rfl)

theorem equations_cons {Y X : Type v} [Finite X] (S : System G Y) (L : Level (GX G Y) X) :
    (cons S X L).equations = Monoid.Coprod.map (.id G) (FreeGroup.map Sum.inr) '' S.equations ∪
      eval (Monoid.Coprod.map (.id G) (FreeGroup.map Sum.inr))
        (fun x ↦ inr (FreeGroup.of (Sum.inl x))) '' L.equations := (rfl)

/-- A raw TQ system is a finite system of equations. -/
theorem finite_equations {Y : Type v} (S : System G Y) : S.equations.Finite := by
  induction S with
  | nil => exact Set.finite_empty
  | cons S X L ih =>
    rw [equations_cons]
    exact (ih.image _).union (L.finite_equations.image _)

/-- A point of `cons S X L` is a point `w = v ∘ Sum.inr` of the lower system `S` together with a
solution `v ∘ Sum.inl` of the top level `L` whose coefficients are evaluated at `w`. -/
theorem mem_V_cons {ι : G →* H} {Y X : Type v} [Finite X] {S : System G Y}
    {L : Level (GX G Y) X} {v : X ⊕ Y → H} : v ∈ V ι (cons S X L).equations ↔
      v ∘ Sum.inr ∈ V ι S.equations ∧ v ∘ Sum.inl ∈ V (eval ι (v ∘ Sum.inr)) L.equations := by
  have h₁ (w : GX G Y) :
      eval ι v (Monoid.Coprod.map (.id G) (FreeGroup.map Sum.inr) w) = eval ι (v ∘ Sum.inr) w := by
    rw [eval_map, MonoidHom.comp_id]
  have h₂ (w : GX (GX G Y) X) :
      eval ι v (eval (Monoid.Coprod.map (.id G) (FreeGroup.map Sum.inr))
        (fun x ↦ inr (FreeGroup.of (Sum.inl x))) w) =
        eval (eval ι (v ∘ Sum.inr)) (v ∘ Sum.inl) w := by
    rw [← MonoidHom.comp_apply, MonoidHom.comp_eval, eval_comp_map, MonoidHom.comp_id]
    simp [Function.comp_def]
  simp only [equations_cons, V_union, Set.mem_inter_iff, mem_V, Set.forall_mem_image, h₁, h₂]

variable (G) in
/-- The coordinate group `G_{R_G(S)} = G[Y] ⧸ Rad_G(S)` of a raw TQ system, the radical being
taken over `G`. The raw lower group of the top level of `cons S X L` is `S.CoordGroup`. -/
abbrev CoordGroup {Y : Type v} (S : System G Y) : Type _ :=
  GroupAlgGeom.CoordGroup (MonoidHom.id G) S.equations

private theorem Rad_nil :
    Rad (MonoidHom.id G) (nil : System G PEmpty).equations =
      (GX.equivOfIsEmpty : GX G PEmpty ≃* G).toMonoidHom.ker := by
  ext w
  -- With no variables, evaluation at the unique point is the identification `G[∅] ≃* G`.
  have h : ∀ v : PEmpty → G, eval (MonoidHom.id G) v w = GX.equivOfIsEmpty w := fun v ↦
    DFunLike.congr_fun (hom_ext (MonoidHom.ext fun g ↦ by simp)
      (FreeGroup.ext_hom _ _ isEmptyElim) :
        eval (MonoidHom.id G) v = GX.equivOfIsEmpty.toMonoidHom) w
  simp [h]

/-- The raw lower group of the bottom level is `G`: the coordinate group of `nil` is
`G[∅] ⧸ Rad_G(∅) ≃* G`. -/
noncomputable def coordGroupNilEquiv : (nil : System G PEmpty).CoordGroup ≃* G :=
  QuotientGroup.liftEquiv _ (MulEquiv.surjective _) Rad_nil

@[simp]
theorem coordGroupNilEquiv_mk (w : GX G PEmpty) :
    coordGroupNilEquiv (w : (nil : System G PEmpty).CoordGroup) = GX.equivOfIsEmpty w := (rfl)

/-- A raw TQ system is *nondegenerate* when each of its levels has a solution in its raw lower
group: `nil` is nondegenerate, and `cons S X L` is nondegenerate when `S` is and the top level
`L`, with its coefficients `G[Y]` read in `G_{R_G(S)}` through the quotient map, has a solution in
`G_{R_G(S)}`. -/
def IsNondegenerate : {Y : Type v} → System G Y → Prop
  | _, nil => True
  | _, cons S _ L => S.IsNondegenerate ∧
      (V (QuotientGroup.mk' (Rad (MonoidHom.id G) S.equations)) L.equations).Nonempty

@[simp]
theorem isNondegenerate_nil : (nil : System G PEmpty).IsNondegenerate := trivial

@[simp]
theorem isNondegenerate_cons {Y X : Type v} [Finite X] {S : System G Y} {L : Level (GX G Y) X} :
    (cons S X L).IsNondegenerate ↔ S.IsNondegenerate ∧
      (V (QuotientGroup.mk' (Rad (MonoidHom.id G) S.equations)) L.equations).Nonempty :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- A level of type (2) never obstructs nondegeneracy: the trivial point solves it. -/
@[simp high]
theorem isNondegenerate_cons_centralizer {Y X : Type v} [Finite X] {S : System G Y}
    {U : Set (GX G Y)} {hU : U.Finite} :
    (cons S X (.centralizer U hU)).IsNondegenerate ↔ S.IsNondegenerate :=
  isNondegenerate_cons.trans <| and_iff_left
    ⟨1, Level.mem_V_centralizer.2 ⟨fun _ _ ↦ .one_left _, fun _ _ _ ↦ .one_left _⟩⟩

/-- A level of type (3) never obstructs nondegeneracy: the trivial point solves it. -/
@[simp high]
theorem isNondegenerate_cons_abelian {Y X : Type v} [Finite X] {S : System G Y} :
    (cons S X .abelian).IsNondegenerate ↔ S.IsNondegenerate :=
  isNondegenerate_cons.trans <| and_iff_left ⟨1, Level.mem_V_abelian.2 fun _ _ ↦ .one_left _⟩

/-- A level of type (4) never obstructs nondegeneracy. -/
@[simp high]
theorem isNondegenerate_cons_empty {Y X : Type v} [Finite X] {S : System G Y} :
    (cons S X .empty).IsNondegenerate ↔ S.IsNondegenerate :=
  isNondegenerate_cons.trans <| and_iff_left <| by simp

end System

/-! ### Admissible centralizer levels -/

section Admissible

variable {H : Type*} [Group H]

/-- Admissible data `(u, U, n)` for a level extending the full centralizer `C_H(u)` of `u` by
`ℤⁿ`: `u` is not a proper power (in particular `u ≠ 1`) and `n > 0`, the centralizer `C_H(u)` is
abelian, and the finite set `U` generates it. -/
structure IsAdmissibleCentralizerLevel (u : H) (U : Finset H) (n : ℕ) : Prop where
  /-- `u` is not a proper power and the added rank `n` is positive. -/
  isAdmissibleCentralizerStep : IsAdmissibleCentralizerStep u n
  /-- The centralizer of `u` is abelian. -/
  isMulCommutative_centralizer : IsMulCommutative (centralizer {u})
  /-- `U` generates the full centralizer of `u`. -/
  closure_eq_centralizer : closure (U : Set H) = centralizer {u}

/-- Admissible centralizer data has a nontrivial element `u`. -/
theorem IsAdmissibleCentralizerLevel.ne_one {u : H} {U : Finset H} {n : ℕ}
    (h : IsAdmissibleCentralizerLevel u U n) : u ≠ 1 :=
  h.isAdmissibleCentralizerStep.ne_one

/-- The identity never gives admissible centralizer data: it is a proper power. -/
theorem not_isAdmissibleCentralizerLevel_one (U : Finset H) (n : ℕ) :
    ¬IsAdmissibleCentralizerLevel (1 : H) U n :=
  fun h ↦ h.ne_one rfl

/-- In a free group, a basis element `a` with `U = {a}` is admissible centralizer data in every
positive rank: its centralizer is the cyclic group it generates. -/
theorem isAdmissibleCentralizerLevel_freeGroup_of {α : Type*} (a : α) {n : ℕ} (hn : 0 < n) :
    IsAdmissibleCentralizerLevel (FreeGroup.of a) {FreeGroup.of a} n where
  isAdmissibleCentralizerStep := isAdmissibleCentralizerStep_freeGroup_of a hn
  isMulCommutative_centralizer := IsFreeGroup.isMulCommutative_centralizer (FreeGroup.of_ne_one a)
  closure_eq_centralizer := by
    rw [Finset.coe_singleton, ← zpowers_eq_closure,
      IsFreeGroup.centralizer_singleton_eq_zpowers_self (FreeGroup.not_isProperPower_of a)]

end Admissible

/-! ### Examples -/

section Examples

/-- Over `F(a, b)`, the one-level system `[x, y] = a`, written as the standard quadratic equation
`[x, y] a⁻¹ = 1` (orientable of genus one, with constant `a⁻¹`), is degenerate: it has no solution
in `F(a, b)`, since `[x, y]` vanishes in the abelianization while `a` does not. -/
theorem not_isNondegenerate_commutator_eq_basis :
    let Q : Quadratic.Standard (GX (FreeGroup (Fin 2)) PEmpty) (Fin 2) :=
      .orientableCoeff 1 0 one_pos ![0] ![1] Fin.elim0 (by decide) Fin.elim0 (fun j ↦ j.elim0)
        (inl (.of 0))⁻¹ (by simp [map_eq_one_iff _ inl_injective, FreeGroup.of_ne_one])
    ¬(System.cons System.nil (Fin 2) (.quadratic Q)).IsNondegenerate := by
  intro Q
  rw [System.isNondegenerate_cons]
  rintro ⟨-, v, hv⟩
  simp only [Level.equations_quadratic, mem_V, Set.mem_singleton_iff, forall_eq] at hv
  -- Map the raw lower group `F(a, b)` onto `ℤ` by `a ↦ 1`, `b ↦ 0`.
  let ψ := (FreeGroup.lift ![Multiplicative.ofAdd (1 : ℤ), 1]).comp
    (System.coordGroupNilEquiv (G := FreeGroup (Fin 2))).toMonoidHom
  have h := DFunLike.congr_fun (MonoidHom.comp_eval ψ (v := v)
    (ι := QuotientGroup.mk' (Rad (MonoidHom.id _) System.nil.equations))) Q.toWord
  simp only [MonoidHom.comp_apply, hv, map_one] at h
  simp [ψ, Q, Quadratic.Standard.toWord_def, commutatorElement_def] at h

/-- Over `F(a, b)`, consider the one-level system `[x, a] = [x, b] = 1`: the level of type (2)
with `U = {a, b}`, a generating set of the full centralizer `C(1) = F(a, b)` of `u = 1`. It is
nondegenerate (`System.isNondegenerate_cons_centralizer`, with the solution `x = 1`), but the data
`u = 1` is not admissible (`not_isAdmissibleCentralizerLevel_one`). Its radical is strictly larger
than the normal closure of its equations: the radical contains `x`, since only `x = 1` commutes
with both `a` and `b`, while the normal closure does not, since `x = (1, 1)` is a solution in
`F(a, b) × ℤ`. So the group defined by the system differs from its coordinate group. -/
theorem normalClosure_lt_Rad_commute_basis :
    let S : System (FreeGroup (Fin 2)) (Unit ⊕ PEmpty) :=
      .cons .nil Unit (.centralizer {inl (.of 0), inl (.of 1)} (Set.toFinite _))
    normalClosure S.equations < Rad (MonoidHom.id _) S.equations := by
  intro S
  refine IsConcreteLE.lt_iff_le_and_exists.2 ⟨normalClosure_le_Rad _,
    inr (FreeGroup.of (Sum.inl ())), mem_Rad.2 fun v hv ↦ ?_, fun hx ↦ ?_⟩
  · -- An element of `F(a, b)` commuting with `a` and `b` is central, hence trivial.
    rw [System.mem_V_cons, Level.mem_V_centralizer] at hv
    have hc : v (Sum.inl ()) ∈ centralizer (Set.range FreeGroup.of) := by
      rw [mem_centralizer_iff]
      rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
      fin_cases i
      · simpa using (hv.2.2 () _ (Set.mem_insert _ _)).eq.symm
      · simpa using (hv.2.2 () _ (Set.mem_insert_of_mem _ rfl)).eq.symm
    rw [← centralizer_closure, FreeGroup.closure_range_of, coe_top, centralizer_univ,
      FreeGroup.center_eq_bot_of_nontrivial, mem_bot] at hc
    simpa using hc
  · -- The point `x = (1, 1)` of `F(a, b) × ℤ` solves the system without killing `x`.
    let ι : FreeGroup (Fin 2) →* FreeGroup (Fin 2) × Multiplicative ℤ := MonoidHom.inl _ _
    have hp : (fun _ ↦ (1, .ofAdd 1)) ∈ V ι S.equations := by
      rw [System.mem_V_cons, Level.mem_V_centralizer]
      refine ⟨by simp, fun _ _ ↦ Commute.refl _, fun _ c _ ↦ ?_⟩
      exact Prod.ext (Commute.one_left _).eq (Commute.all _ _).eq
    have := mem_Rad.1 ((normalClosure_le_Rad (ι := ι) S.equations) hx) _ hp
    simp at this

/-- The two-level system with lower level `[u, v] = 1` (of type (3)) and upper level the standard
quadratic equation `x⁻¹ u x · u⁻¹ = 1` (orientable of genus zero, with coefficients `c = u` and
`d = u⁻¹` in the lower variables) is nondegenerate: the lower level is solved in `G` by
`u = v = 1`, and the upper level is solved in the coordinate group of the lower level by `x = 1`,
its coefficients remaining the images of `u` and `u⁻¹` in that group. -/
theorem isNondegenerate_conj_over_commute {G : Type*} [Group G] :
    let Q : Quadratic.Standard (GX G (Fin 2 ⊕ PEmpty)) Unit :=
      .orientableCoeff 0 1 one_pos Fin.elim0 Fin.elim0 (fun _ ↦ ()) (by decide)
        (fun _ ↦ inr (.of (.inl 0)))
        (fun _ ↦ by simp [map_eq_one_iff _ inr_injective, FreeGroup.of_ne_one])
        (inr (.of (.inl 0)))⁻¹ (by simp [map_eq_one_iff _ inr_injective, FreeGroup.of_ne_one])
    (System.cons (System.cons System.nil (Fin 2) .abelian) Unit
      (.quadratic Q)).IsNondegenerate := by
  intro Q
  refine System.isNondegenerate_cons.2
    ⟨System.isNondegenerate_cons_abelian.2 System.isNondegenerate_nil, 1, ?_⟩
  simp [Q, Quadratic.Standard.toWord_def]

end Examples

end TauCeti.LimitGroup.NTQ
